insert into public.court_verdict_templates (
  case_id,outcome_key,headline,what_court_heard,verdict,court_ordered_move,share_text,tone_condition
) values
('CASE-028','spectrum_1','COLD + COLD','You both run hot and want the place practically refrigerated.','No thermostat battle here — the risk is just an electric bill nobody wants to look at.','[username A] sentenced to: check the thermostat setting once this week before blasting the AC out of habit. [username B] sentenced to: same — your turn to notice. Agree on one temperature number you''ll both default to, so neither of you keeps nudging it down out of habit.','Bunny Court closed Thermostat Wars.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-028','spectrum_2','COLD + BALANCED','One of you wants it cold, practically arctic. The other''s fine either way.','Easy compromise territory — the balanced partner has more room to flex toward "cold" without it costing them much.','[Cold-preferring username] sentenced to: keep a blanket nearby instead of cranking the thermostat every time. [Balanced username] sentenced to: let the temp sit a couple degrees cooler than your personal default. Find one middle-ground number this week and just leave it there for a few days, see how it feels.','Bunny Court closed Thermostat Wars.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-028','spectrum_3','COLD + WARM','One of you wants the place cold enough to see your breath. The other wants a sweater-optional zone.','This is a genuinely opposite preference, not a personality flaw — someone''s always going to be slightly off from their ideal here.','[Cold-preferring username] sentenced to: keep a fan or personal cooling setup instead of controlling the whole room''s temp. [Warm-preferring username] sentenced to: keep a blanket and slippers on standby instead of touching the thermostat every hour. Split the day into "your zone hours" — pick a time block each where the room runs at your preferred temp.','Bunny Court closed Thermostat Wars.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-028','spectrum_4','BALANCED + BALANCED','Neither of you has strong feelings about the thermostat — this might genuinely be your most peaceful household decision.','No conflict, no notes, mildly impressive.','[username A] sentenced to: pick this week''s temperature, no debate needed. [username B] sentenced to: your turn next week. Rotate who picks the temp each week — see if either of you even notices a difference.','Bunny Court closed Thermostat Wars.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-028','spectrum_5','BALANCED + WARM','One of you doesn''t care much either way. The other genuinely needs it warm to be comfortable.','Low-friction fix — the balanced partner has room to lean warm without much personal cost.','[Balanced username] sentenced to: let the temp run a couple degrees warmer than your default. [Warm-preferring username] sentenced to: keep a fan nearby for the rare moments it does feel too warm. Set the thermostat to the warm-preferring partner''s ideal for a week and see if the balanced partner even notices.','Bunny Court closed Thermostat Wars.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-028','spectrum_6','WARM + WARM','You both want the place warm enough to skip socks entirely.','No thermostat war here — just make sure the heating bill doesn''t become its own courtroom drama.','[username A] sentenced to: check the setting once this week before turning up the heat out of habit. [username B] sentenced to: same. Agree on one shared temperature number so neither of you keeps nudging it up.','Bunny Court closed Thermostat Wars.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-032','spectrum_1','EARLY + EARLY','You''re both up with the sun and asleep before anything interesting happens on TV.','Rare synced schedules — the only risk is losing touch with anyone who isn''t a morning person.','[username A] sentenced to: stay up 30 minutes past your usual bedtime once this week, together. [username B] sentenced to: same — no falling asleep on the couch. Plan one "late night" this week — even 10pm counts as adventurous for you two.','Bunny Court closed Early Bird vs Night Owl Court.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-032','spectrum_2','EARLY + BALANCED','One of you is up at dawn no matter what. The other can swing either way depending on the day.','Easy overlap here — the balanced partner has the flexibility to meet the early riser without much sacrifice.','[Early-leaning username] sentenced to: let one morning plan slide for a slower start. [Balanced username] sentenced to: join the early plan without complaint at least once this week. Pick one morning activity to do together this week — coffee, a walk, anything before noon.','Bunny Court closed Early Bird vs Night Owl Court.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-032','spectrum_3','EARLY + NIGHT','One of you is winding down right when the other is just getting going.','Genuinely different internal clocks, not a compatibility red flag — plenty of couples run on opposite schedules just fine.','[Early-leaning username] sentenced to: stay up a little later once this week to catch some overlap time. [Night-leaning username] sentenced to: get up a little earlier once this week to do the same. Find one hour that works for both clocks and protect it as your dedicated overlap time.','Bunny Court closed Early Bird vs Night Owl Court.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-032','spectrum_4','BALANCED + BALANCED','Neither of you is locked into a rigid schedule — you both adjust pretty easily.','No real conflict here, refreshingly low-maintenance.','[username A] sentenced to: pick the wake-up time this week. [username B] sentenced to: pick it next week. Try syncing your schedules for one full day and see how it feels compared to your usual flexible routine.','Bunny Court closed Early Bird vs Night Owl Court.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-032','spectrum_5','BALANCED + NIGHT','One of you can go either way. The other genuinely comes alive after dark.','Manageable gap — the balanced partner has the flexibility to lean into later hours without much cost.','[Balanced username] sentenced to: stay up a bit later once this week to catch some overlap. [Night-leaning username] sentenced to: get up slightly earlier once, just to share a morning. Plan a late-night activity together this week that plays to the night owl''s actual prime time.','Bunny Court closed Early Bird vs Night Owl Court.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-032','spectrum_6','NIGHT + NIGHT','You''re both wide awake when the rest of the world''s asleep, and useless before 10am.','No clash here — just watch out for mornings sneaking up on you as a household.','[username A] sentenced to: set one alarm this week for something that actually matters. [username B] sentenced to: same — no snoozing through it together. Plan one genuinely great late-night activity this week — this is your prime time, use it.','Bunny Court closed Early Bird vs Night Owl Court.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-037','spectrum_1','COOK + COOK','You both genuinely prefer cooking — takeout apps barely get opened in this household.','No conflict here, just two people who''d rather chop vegetables than scroll a delivery app.','[username A] sentenced to: pick this week''s menu. [username B] sentenced to: handle the dishes, no negotiating. Try one new recipe together this week, split the labor down the middle.','Bunny Court closed Takeout vs Home-Cooked Tribunal.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-037','spectrum_2','COOK + BALANCED','One of you defaults to cooking. The other''s happy either way, cooking or ordering in.','Not a conflict — the balanced partner has room to lean into cooking more without much sacrifice.','[Cook-leaning username] sentenced to: let one night be takeout without guilt. [Balanced username] sentenced to: help with one home-cooked meal this week, prep or cleanup, your choice. Plan the week''s meals together — a mix of both, decided in advance instead of last-minute.','Bunny Court closed Takeout vs Home-Cooked Tribunal.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-037','spectrum_3','COOK + TAKEOUT','One of you would cook every night if there were time. The other''s default is "let''s just order."','This isn''t laziness versus effort — one of you finds cooking relaxing, the other finds convenience more valuable than time in the kitchen. Both are legitimate ways to handle dinner.','[Cook-leaning username] sentenced to: agree to a set number of takeout nights per week without side-eyeing it. [Takeout-leaning username] sentenced to: commit to one home-cooked night, even if it''s a simple one. Pick one easy recipe you both actually enjoy making, so "cooking" doesn''t always mean a big production.','Bunny Court closed Takeout vs Home-Cooked Tribunal.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-037','spectrum_4','BALANCED + BALANCED','Neither of you has a strong default — dinner just happens based on the day, no real pattern.','No conflict, refreshingly low-maintenance around here.','[username A] sentenced to: plan tonight''s dinner, whatever it is. [username B] sentenced to: no complaints about the choice. Do a "surprise me" dinner night — one of you decides, the other just goes with it.','Bunny Court closed Takeout vs Home-Cooked Tribunal.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-037','spectrum_5','BALANCED + TAKEOUT','One of you is fine either way. The other genuinely leans toward ordering in as the default.','Low-friction gap — the balanced partner has room to go along with takeout more often without much cost.','[Balanced username] sentenced to: suggest cooking once this week, just to keep the option alive. [Takeout-leaning username] sentenced to: say yes to it without much resistance. Try one "lazy cooking" night — something that takes 15 minutes, splitting the difference.','Bunny Court closed Takeout vs Home-Cooked Tribunal.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-037','spectrum_6','TAKEOUT + TAKEOUT','You both default to ordering in — the kitchen mostly exists for reheating leftovers.','No conflict between you, but the court gently notes your delivery app probably has your order memorized.','[username A] sentenced to: cook one simple meal this month, no pressure. [username B] sentenced to: help, don''t just supervise. Pick one ridiculously easy recipe and make it together, just to remember the stove exists.','Bunny Court closed Takeout vs Home-Cooked Tribunal.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-039','spectrum_1','INDEPENDENT + INDEPENDENT','You both genuinely value having a full life outside the relationship — friend time isn''t something either of you has to fight for.','No conflict here, healthy independence on both sides.','[username A] sentenced to: plan one friend hang this week without guilt. [username B] sentenced to: same. Compare calendars and make sure at least one dedicated us-night still makes it onto the schedule.','Bunny Court closed Friend Time vs Us Time Ratio.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-039','spectrum_2','INDEPENDENT + BALANCED','One of you needs regular independent time with friends. The other''s fine with however much or little happens.','Not a conflict — the balanced partner has flexibility to support the independent one''s need for space without feeling shortchanged.','[Independent-leaning username] sentenced to: make sure friend time doesn''t quietly eat into planned us-time. [Balanced username] sentenced to: use some of that freed-up time for their own thing too, not just waiting around. Plan one guaranteed us-night this week that doesn''t get bumped for anything.','Bunny Court closed Friend Time vs Us Time Ratio.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-039','spectrum_3','INDEPENDENT + COUPLE-LEANING','One of you needs regular time with friends to feel like yourself. The other feels most connected when it''s just the two of you.','Neither need is wrong — one of you recharges through your own social world, the other recharges through the relationship itself.','[Independent-leaning username] sentenced to: give a heads-up before friend plans instead of springing them last-minute. [Couple-leaning username] sentenced to: use that freed-up time for something of your own instead of just missing them. Set a recurring, non-negotiable us-night each week, so independent time never has to come at its expense.','Bunny Court closed Friend Time vs Us Time Ratio.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-039','spectrum_4','BALANCED + BALANCED','Neither of you has strong feelings about the friend-time-to-us-time ratio — it just balances out naturally.','No conflict here, this is a pretty enviable equilibrium.','[username A] sentenced to: plan a friend hang this week, doesn''t matter which. [username B] sentenced to: plan an us-night too. Do a joint hangout with friends this week — best of both worlds.','Bunny Court closed Friend Time vs Us Time Ratio.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-039','spectrum_5','BALANCED + COUPLE-LEANING','One of you is fine either way. The other genuinely prefers most free time to go toward the relationship.','Low-friction gap — the balanced partner has room to lean into more us-time without much cost.','[Balanced username] sentenced to: prioritize an us-night this week over a lower-stakes friend hang. [Couple-leaning username] sentenced to: encourage one solo friend hang for your partner, even if it''s not your instinct. Plan a date night this week that feels intentional, not just leftover time.','Bunny Court closed Friend Time vs Us Time Ratio.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-039','spectrum_6','COUPLE-LEANING + COUPLE-LEANING','You both genuinely prefer spending most free time together — friend hangouts happen, just less often.','No conflict here, this works for plenty of couples.','[username A] sentenced to: reach out to one friend this week, just to keep that muscle alive. [username B] sentenced to: same. Invite friends to join one of your usual date nights this week, just to mix it up.','Bunny Court closed Friend Time vs Us Time Ratio.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-040','spectrum_1','PACKED + PACKED','You''re both the type to plan every hour of a trip — downtime feels like wasted vacation to either of you.','No mismatch, just two overachievers on vacation.','[username A] sentenced to: build in one unplanned hour, just to see what happens. [username B] sentenced to: same. Plan your next trip''s itinerary together, hour by hour — you''ll both actually enjoy doing that part.','Bunny Court closed The Group Trip Itinerary Case.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-040','spectrum_2','PACKED + BALANCED','One of you wants a packed itinerary. The other''s fine with a loose plan either way.','Not a conflict — the balanced partner has flexibility to go along with a fuller schedule without burning out.','[Packed-leaning username] sentenced to: build in one buffer hour with nothing planned. [Balanced username] sentenced to: speak up if the pace actually feels like too much. Plan the trip''s must-do list together, then leave the rest open.','Bunny Court closed The Group Trip Itinerary Case.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-040','spectrum_3','PACKED + CHILL','One of you wants every hour of the trip mapped out. The other just wants to see where the day takes them.','Neither approach is wrong — one of you gets energy from doing, the other gets energy from resting. Vacation just means different things to each of you.','[Packed-leaning username] sentenced to: build in at least one full unplanned day. [Chill-leaning username] sentenced to: commit to one or two must-do activities without pushback. Split the trip — plan half the days together in detail, leave the other half totally open.','Bunny Court closed The Group Trip Itinerary Case.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-040','spectrum_4','BALANCED + BALANCED','Neither of you needs a strict itinerary or total chaos — trips just tend to work themselves out.','No conflict, easygoing travel duo.','[username A] sentenced to: pick one activity for the trip. [username B] sentenced to: pick another. Plan just the flights and one activity — let the rest unfold naturally.','Bunny Court closed The Group Trip Itinerary Case.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-040','spectrum_5','BALANCED + CHILL','One of you doesn''t care much about the pace. The other genuinely wants a relaxed, unscheduled trip.','Low-friction gap — the balanced partner has room to slow down without much sacrifice.','[Balanced username] sentenced to: resist the urge to overplan the itinerary. [Chill-leaning username] sentenced to: pick one must-do thing so it''s not entirely open-ended. Plan a trip with literally one fixed activity and see how the rest of the time feels.','Bunny Court closed The Group Trip Itinerary Case.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-040','spectrum_6','CHILL + CHILL','You both just want to show up and relax — itineraries feel like unnecessary homework to either of you.','No conflict here, you''re both built for the same kind of vacation.','[username A] sentenced to: book one (1) activity in advance, just so the trip has a highlight. [username B] sentenced to: show up to it. Plan your next trip with zero itinerary and see how it goes — you''ll probably love it.','Bunny Court closed The Group Trip Itinerary Case.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-042','spectrum_1','PROPORTIONAL + PROPORTIONAL','You both think the split should scale with income — whoever earns more contributes more.','You''re aligned here, which makes this one of the easier financial conversations a couple can have.','[username A] sentenced to: revisit the split percentages if either income changes. [username B] sentenced to: same. Sit down once and actually calculate the proportional split together, so it''s explicit instead of assumed.','Bunny Court closed The Budget Split Verdict.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-042','spectrum_2','PROPORTIONAL + BALANCED','One of you thinks the split should track income. The other''s flexible, leaning proportional for big stuff, even for small.','Not really a conflict — you''re both already pretty close on this one.','[Proportional-leaning username] sentenced to: clarify which expenses actually need the proportional split versus which can just be split evenly. [Balanced username] sentenced to: go along with the proportional model where it makes sense. Pick one recurring expense and agree on how it''ll be split going forward, as a test case.','Bunny Court closed The Budget Split Verdict.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-042','spectrum_3','PROPORTIONAL + EQUAL-SPLIT','One of you thinks the split should scale with income. The other believes 50/50 is what''s fair, regardless of who earns what.','Neither model is inherently more fair — proportional split protects the lower earner''s lifestyle, 50/50 protects a sense of equal ownership. The disagreement is really about what "fair" means to each of you.','[Proportional-leaning username] sentenced to: explain what specifically feels unfair about strict 50/50, beyond just the math. [Equal-split-leaning username] sentenced to: explain what 50/50 represents to you beyond the numbers. Try a hybrid split for one month — proportional on big expenses, 50/50 on small ones — and see how it feels.','Bunny Court closed The Budget Split Verdict.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-042','spectrum_4','BALANCED + BALANCED','Neither of you has a strong stance on the exact split model — you both just want something that feels fair enough.','No conflict, this case barely needed a hearing.','[username A] sentenced to: check in on the current split once this month. [username B] sentenced to: bring actual numbers, not vibes. Do a quick shared-expenses review together this month, just to make sure "fair enough" still feels that way.','Bunny Court closed The Budget Split Verdict.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-042','spectrum_5','BALANCED + EQUAL-SPLIT','One of you doesn''t have a strong preference. The other genuinely wants a strict 50/50 split.','Low-friction gap — the balanced partner can go along with 50/50 without much cost.','[Balanced username] sentenced to: agree to the 50/50 model without pushing for proportional. [Equal-split-leaning username] sentenced to: revisit it if the income gap grows significantly over time. Set the 50/50 split explicitly for shared expenses this month and check in on how it feels.','Bunny Court closed The Budget Split Verdict.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-042','spectrum_6','EQUAL-SPLIT + EQUAL-SPLIT','You both believe in strict 50/50, no matter the income difference between you.','No conflict here — this model works fine as long as it doesn''t create financial strain for either of you.','[username A] sentenced to: flag it honestly if 50/50 ever starts to feel like a stretch. [username B] sentenced to: take that seriously if it comes up. Revisit the 50/50 agreement once a year, just to make sure it still works for both of you.','Bunny Court closed The Budget Split Verdict.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-044','spectrum_1','EXTROVERT + EXTROVERT','You''re both the "let''s find something to do" type — staying in on a free Friday feels like a missed opportunity to either of you.','No mismatch, matched energy levels, socially speaking.','[username A] sentenced to: plan tonight''s outing. [username B] sentenced to: pick the group to invite. Say yes to the next spontaneous plan that comes up, no discussion needed.','Bunny Court closed The Thermostat of Social Battery.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-044','spectrum_2','EXTROVERT + BALANCED','One of you wants to be out and about most weekends. The other can go either way depending on energy levels.','Not a conflict — the balanced partner has flexibility to go along with plans without it draining them.','[Extrovert-leaning username] sentenced to: read the room if your partner seems tapped out. [Balanced username] sentenced to: say yes to the outing this week if you''re genuinely up for it. Plan one low-effort outing this week — something social, but not draining.','Bunny Court closed The Thermostat of Social Battery.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-044','spectrum_3','EXTROVERT + INTROVERT','One of you needs to be out and around people to feel recharged. The other needs quiet and alone time to feel human again.','Neither battery type is wrong — one of you refuels through stimulation, the other through stillness.','[Extrovert-leaning username] sentenced to: go do the social thing solo or with friends sometimes, instead of always waiting for buy-in. [Introvert-leaning username] sentenced to: give a heads-up when you''re at your limit, instead of just going quiet. Alternate weekends — one that''s more social, one that''s fully low-key — and see how the rhythm feels.','Bunny Court closed The Thermostat of Social Battery.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-044','spectrum_4','BALANCED + BALANCED','Neither of you has a strong social battery preference — some weekends you''re out, some you''re in, no real pattern.','No conflict here, genuinely adaptable pairing.','[username A] sentenced to: pick this weekend''s vibe. [username B] sentenced to: go along with it. Alternate who decides "in or out" each weekend, just to keep it fair.','Bunny Court closed The Thermostat of Social Battery.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-044','spectrum_5','BALANCED + INTROVERT','One of you can go either way. The other genuinely needs more quiet time to recharge.','Low-friction gap — the balanced partner has room to stay in more without much cost.','[Balanced username] sentenced to: suggest a night out occasionally, but don''t push if it''s a hard no. [Introvert-leaning username] sentenced to: say yes to one low-key outing this month. Plan a quiet at-home night that still feels intentional, not just "nothing happening."','Bunny Court closed The Thermostat of Social Battery.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-044','spectrum_6','INTROVERT + INTROVERT','You both recharge best at home — Friday nights are for the couch, not the calendar.','No conflict, this works fine, plenty of couples run quiet.','[username A] sentenced to: make one plan outside the house this month. [username B] sentenced to: show up to it without dread. Pick one small outing this month that feels manageable, just to keep a foot in the world.','Bunny Court closed The Thermostat of Social Battery.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-027','spectrum_1','TOGETHER + TOGETHER','You both wish you saw each other even more than you already do — if anything, the "problem" here is scheduling, not desire.','Rare case where the court has nothing to referee — you''re both pulling in the same direction. Just don''t let "we''ll see each other eventually" become the plan.','[username A] sentenced to: block off one no-cancel hangout this week, calendar invite and all. [username B] sentenced to: same, but you pick the activity this time. Plan one thing further out than usual — a trip, an event, something to look forward to together, not just this week''s hangout.','Bunny Court closed The Great Hangout Frequency Case.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-027','spectrum_2','TOGETHER + BALANCED','One of you would happily see each other daily. The other''s content with a steady rhythm — not desperate for more, not needing less.','Not a mismatch, just different appetites — the balanced partner has more flexibility here to meet in the middle without it costing them much.','[Together-leaning username] sentenced to: fill the extra "want-to-see-you" energy with a solo hobby or friend hang, not just waiting around. [Balanced username] sentenced to: say yes to one extra hangout this week that you wouldn''t have initiated yourself. Agree on a "standing" hangout day that happens no matter what — takes the guesswork out for the one who wants more certainty.','Bunny Court closed The Great Hangout Frequency Case.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-027','spectrum_3','TOGETHER + SPACE（已确认案例）','One of you wants daily check-ins. The other needs some breathing room in between.','Different social batteries, not different levels of caring — one of you refuels around people, the other refuels alone. Both are valid, neither is "too much" or "too distant."','[username A] sentenced to: lock in 2 non-negotiable hangouts this week on the calendar. [username B] sentenced to: give 24hr notice instead of a last-minute cancel if a plan needs to move. Pick one small recurring ritual just for you two — Sunday coffee, no-phone walk, whatever — something that happens on repeat, no re-planning needed every time.','Bunny Court closed The Great Hangout Frequency Case.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-027','spectrum_4','BALANCED + BALANCED','Neither of you is pushing for more or asking for space — your rhythm''s already working. This case is basically a formality.','The court finds you both refreshingly reasonable. The only risk with "it''s fine as is" is coasting without noticing when it stops being fine.','[username A] sentenced to: check in once this month — "are we still doing enough of this?" [username B] sentenced to: actually answer honestly instead of saying "yeah we''re good" on autopilot. Once a month, do a 5-minute "relationship check-in" — no agenda, just "how are we doing on time together?"','Bunny Court closed The Great Hangout Frequency Case.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-027','spectrum_5','BALANCED + SPACE','One of you is fine with the current pace. The other genuinely needs more space between hangouts to recharge.','The one who needs space isn''t pulling away from the relationship — they''re just wired to need more solo recovery time. The balanced partner has room to flex toward that without losing much.','[Balanced username] sentenced to: let one plan get pushed back without taking it personally. [Space-leaning username] sentenced to: give a heads-up when you need a lower-key week, instead of just going quiet on plans. Agree on a simple signal for "I need a quieter week" so it never reads as distance.','Bunny Court closed The Great Hangout Frequency Case.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('CASE-027','spectrum_6','SPACE + SPACE','You''re both perfectly happy with a lighter rhythm — this isn''t a couple who needs to be glued together to feel connected.','No note from the court here — some couples run on a slower cadence and it works fine. Just make sure "low-key" doesn''t quietly turn into "barely."','[username A] sentenced to: pick one date this month that''s non-negotiable, even on a light week. [username B] sentenced to: same — your turn to pick the date. Once a season, do something bigger than your usual low-key hangout — dial up the effort once in a while.','Bunny Court closed The Great Hangout Frequency Case.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-02','sink_in_balance','SINK IN BALANCE','The dishes are noticed, handled, and returned to cabinet society without one person filing repeated notices.','The Court finds a functional cleanup ecosystem. Protect it from the dangerous phrase “I thought you were doing it.”','`[username A]` takes the least favorite step next meal. `[username B]` closes the kitchen completely—counter included. Race one ten-minute reset with a three-song soundtrack.','The sponge has rested its case.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-02','one_person_cleanup_crew','ONE-PERSON CLEANUP CREW','One person has become the sink’s emergency contact. The other may contribute, but usually after the work has been noticed, named, or nearly finished.','The imbalance is not only washing; it is carrying the reminder system. The Court transfers one full cleanup cycle, including noticing.','The usual non-starter owns the next meal’s cleanup from first plate to final counter. The usual cleaner does not supervise unless sanitation law is genuinely at risk. Choose a repeatable rule: cook rests, alternate nights, or fixed lanes.','Reminder duty has been removed from the sink.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-02','two_conflicting_dish_documentaries','TWO CONFLICTING DISH DOCUMENTARIES','Both people remember contributing, and both somehow remember doing more. The missing footage is probably “mental load: the prequel.”','This is a definition dispute: doing one visible step versus owning the whole task. The Court orders roles with obvious finish lines.','Each names the step they currently count as “doing dishes.” Then each claims one complete lane with no invisible handoff. Test the new split for three meals, then keep or swap lanes.','The sink accepts no vague promises. ---','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-03','remote_peace_treaty','REMOTE PEACE TREATY','The remote changes hands, vetoes stay humane, and both people occasionally watch something they did not personally commission.','Shared taste is optional; a trusted selection process is enough. Yours appears to be functioning.','`[username A]` picks the next episode night. `[username B]` supplies snacks and one no-eye-roll episode of good faith. Each nominate one show and choose by trailer, not a forty-five-minute scroll.','Autoplay is the only remaining suspect.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-03','taste_gap_easy_rotation','TASTE GAP, EASY ROTATION','One person wants prestige drama; the other wants something that can survive snack noise. Neither taste is leaving voluntarily.','The Court orders rotation, not cultural conversion. A one-episode trial prevents both dictatorship and endless negotiation.','The frequent chooser gives the next pick away without lobbying. The next chooser selects something reasonably shared, saving niche punishment for solo hours. Build three lists: yours, mine, and genuinely ours.','Genre differences remain legally entertaining.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-03','browsing_night_deadlock','BROWSING-NIGHT DEADLOCK','The remote is technically shared, but one person supplies all options while the other rejects them from a comfortable distance.','“I don’t care” followed by six vetoes is a form of governance. Decision labor now rotates with the remote.','The habitual vetoer brings three choices next time. The habitual planner accepts one without opening a rival selection process. Use a three-option cap and a five-minute timer.','The thumbnails may stop interviewing for the role. ---','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-04','cart_in_balance','CART IN BALANCE','Food appears through recognizable teamwork rather than household magic. The list and the labor both have owners.','The grocery system works. The Court requests only continued snack diplomacy.','`[username A]` adds one item `[username B]` likes without being asked. `[username B]` handles put-away completely next run. Do one ten-minute list check before the next shop.','The oversized cart has been released from custody.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-04','one_person_logistics_department','ONE-PERSON LOGISTICS DEPARTMENT','One person knows what is missing, plans the run, remembers preferences, and may also carry the bags while someone asks where the cereal lives.','The imbalance begins before the store. The Court assigns one full run, including inventory and put-away, to the less frequent owner.','The new owner plans and completes the next run. The usual owner provides dietary facts once, then leaves management alone. Keep one shared live list where both people add items when they finish them.','Groceries will no longer spawn through unpaid lore.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-04','aisle_level_confusion','AISLE-LEVEL CONFUSION','Both people help, but one means “buy food” while the other means “forecast every meal and compare three oat milks.”','Effort is present; definitions are not. A clean handoff will prevent two partial jobs from becoming one annoyed person.','One partner owns list and budget; the other owns shop and put-away. Swap next time if the split proves cursed. Agree on essentials, flexible choices, and one chaos snack.','Receipt admitted; resentment removed from the bagging area. ---','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-06','laundry_peace_accords','LAUNDRY PEACE ACCORDS','Clothes travel from hamper to drawer without entering a long-term relationship with nearby furniture.','The Court recognizes a rare full-cycle laundry system. Continue until the fitted sheet files an appeal.','`[username A]` handles the next annoying specialty item. `[username B]` closes the final put-away step. Fold one load together before the playlist ends.','The chair pile will not be called as a witness.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-06','one_person_carries_the_basket','ONE PERSON CARRIES THE BASKET','One person is doing more than fabric care; they are also tracking timing, rescuing damp loads, and reminding the household that drawers exist.','Partial help does not equal task ownership. The Court transfers one full cycle with no reminder subscription.','The lighter-load partner owns the next load from sorting through put-away. The usual owner does not redo folds for aesthetic reasons unless asked. Pick one recurring load that permanently belongs to each person.','Mental load removed from the delicate cycle.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-06','competing_definitions_of_done','COMPETING DEFINITIONS OF DONE','One person believes “dry” means complete. The other is standing beside a clean mountain asking where their socks went.','Nobody is lying; your finish lines are simply several rooms apart. A task needs one shared definition before it can be shared fairly.','Each chooses a full-cycle lane or explicitly trades stages. No abandoned handoffs without notice. Write the four-step finish line once and choose who owns each step this week.','“Technically clean” is no longer a complete defense. ---','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-08','co_parenting_the_creature','CO-PARENTING THE CREATURE','Care is shared, the dependent appears alive, and neither person is using cute photos as proof of operational contribution.','The Court finds competent joint custody. Continue monitoring snacks, water, walks, and dramatic leaf posture.','`[username A]` takes the next unpleasant task. `[username B]` checks supplies before they become an emergency. Do one care task together and review the routine in five minutes.','The dependent declined comment but appears hydrated.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-08','primary_caretaker_identified','PRIMARY CARETAKER IDENTIFIED','One person carries the schedule, the supplies, and most of the actual care. The other loves the dependent but has been cast mainly in lifestyle photography.','Affection is welcome; dependents still require completed tasks. The Court assigns recurring ownership rather than occasional rescue help.','The secondary caretaker claims one daily and one weekly task. The primary caretaker communicates the standard once, then allows real ownership. Put named tasks and backup coverage somewhere visible.','Cute photos now require supporting documentation.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-08','care_plan_needs_adult_supervision','CARE PLAN NEEDS ADULT SUPERVISION','Tasks are being missed, assumed, or completed to incompatible standards. A living thing has become the least amusing part of the disagreement.','Welfare outranks fairness theatre. The care plan must become explicit today, with outside help if neither schedule can safely hold it.','One partner handles the immediate missed need. The other arranges the durable fix—reminder, sitter, vet, supplies, or schedule change. Build a minimum-care checklist and name an emergency backup.','The dependent is the only party with veto power. ---','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-10','fair_mileage','FAIR MILEAGE','The wheel changes hands—or stays with the preferred driver—without accumulating emotional toll charges.','The current arrangement is fair because both people actually agree it is, not because nobody has raised the issue at highway speed.','`[username A]` takes the next support job seriously. `[username B]` checks fuel, route, or breaks before departure. Plan one drive where driver and passenger roles are chosen in advance.','Mileage accepted; backseat commentary pending.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-10','designated_driver_willing_passenger','DESIGNATED DRIVER, WILLING PASSENGER','One person genuinely prefers driving. The other has built a respectable career in navigation, snacks, music, and suspiciously timed naps.','Equal does not always mean equal wheel time. It means the support role is real and the driver can request relief without filing paperwork.','The passenger owns route, parking research, and one useful stop. The driver asks for a swap before exhaustion, not after martyrdom. Trade roles for one short, low-stress trip if both feel safe doing so.','Passenger-princess status renewed with duties.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-10','road_resentment','ROAD RESENTMENT','One person feels stuck driving, judged while driving, or pressured to drive when uncomfortable. The car has become a moving feedback session.','Safety and capacity decide before fairness arithmetic. Criticism without shared responsibility is hereby removed from the vehicle.','The frequent driver names the exact burden: fatigue, mileage, navigation, or commentary. The other takes a safe share or compensating task and limits feedback to actual safety needs. Agree before the next trip on driver, swap point, navigation, and feedback rules.','The car is in park; the argument should be too. ---','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-13','prep_partners','PREP PARTNERS','Containers stack, lunches appear, and both people understand that chopping onions counts as weekend labor.','The Court finds a functional food-production cooperative. Keep the menu varied enough to prevent Thursday despair.','`[username A]` chooses next week’s wildcard meal. `[username B]` owns cleanup and fridge labeling. Prep one base ingredient and customize two different meals from it.','The containers have been stacked in peace.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-13','planner_improviser','PLANNER / IMPROVISER','One person sees future freedom in labeled containers. The other sees five copies of a decision they were not ready to make.','Different planning appetites can share a kitchen. Prep the obligations, leave some room for Tuesday personality changes.','The planner limits prep to agreed staples. The improviser commits to one concrete role and stops treating prepared food as mysteriously occurring inventory. Prep two staples and reserve two open meal slots.','Structure granted; spontaneity kept refrigerated.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-13','sunday_labor_dispute','SUNDAY LABOR DISPUTE','One person loses a large weekend block preparing food both people eat. The other participates mainly at consumption.','Benefiting from a system creates responsibility for the system. The Court assigns labor or permits the cook to scale the service down.','The beneficiary takes shopping plus cleanup, or owns one full prep week. The regular prepper states the minimum help required and stops producing beyond the agreement. Time one real prep session, split the stages, and decide whether the savings justify the labor.','Free lunch found to contain hidden Sunday hours. ---','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-14','calendar_coalition','CALENDAR COALITION','Both parties can see the year ahead without anyone secretly planning an airport breakdown.','The Court approves the existing coalition. Write it down before family group chats begin independent negotiations.','`[username A]` communicates one part of the plan to their family. `[username B]` communicates the matching boundary to theirs. Add one tradition that belongs only to the two of you.','Holiday diplomacy remains operational.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-14','tradition_tug_of_war','TRADITION TUG-OF-WAR','Both people are attached to real relationships and rituals. Unfortunately, the calendar contains fewer holidays than emotional obligations.','Fairness should be measured across years, travel, time, and emotional cost—not by forcing one exhausted day into perfect halves.','Each ranks one must-have and one flexible tradition. Each also takes responsibility for disappointing their own family when compromise requires it. Build a two-year calendar instead of re-litigating each invitation.','Equality may occur over time, not before dessert.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-14','boundary_at_the_dinner_table','BOUNDARY AT THE DINNER TABLE','This is not merely scheduling. One option carries hostility, unsafe travel, financial strain, exclusion, or pressure that the other option does not.','Equal exposure to unequal conditions is not fairness. The Court permits a boundary, separate attendance, or a new tradition without punishment.','The directly connected partner communicates the boundary to their family. The other supports it without turning the moment into a loyalty test. Design the safest, kindest plan for this year and schedule a calm review after the season.','Snacks and emotional flexibility strongly recommended. ---','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-15','mutual_spotters','MUTUAL SPOTTERS','Both people enjoy the invite, the check-in, and at least some of the actual exercise.','Shared accountability is working because it remains voluntary. The Court awards no points for suffering theatrically near a treadmill.','`[username A]` picks the next session. `[username B]` handles timing and post-workout reward. Choose one movement goal and one fun goal for the same session.','The alarm clock has been excused from testimony.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-15','buddy_solo_athlete','BUDDY / SOLO ATHLETE','One person gains energy from a workout partner. The other performs better without being observed, coordinated, or asked how many reps remain.','Support does not have to happen in identical shoes. Build one shared touchpoint around two valid routines.','The buddy-seeker limits invitations to the agreed frequency. The solo exerciser offers one form of support they genuinely enjoy—walk, check-in, or celebration. Share one warm-up, walk, or recovery ritual while keeping the main workout separate.','Different routines, same hydration reminder.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-15','coach_whistle_confiscated','COACH WHISTLE CONFISCATED','Nudges have started sounding like supervision, disappointment, or commentary on effort and bodies.','Accountability requires consent every time its form changes. The Court removes unsolicited coaching from the relationship gym.','The frequent coach asks, “support, company, or no input?” The pressured partner answers directly and does not agree to tracking they do not want. Define one welcome encouragement and two off-limits comments.','Personal trainer credentials were never filed. ---','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-16','calendar_citizenship','CALENDAR CITIZENSHIP','Shared plans enter a shared system, changes appear, and nobody must reconstruct the week from reaction emojis.','The Court recognizes functional calendar citizenship. Continue paying attention to the notifications you requested.','`[username A]` adds the next shared plan with details. `[username B]` records the next change rather than announcing it into the air. Review the next seven days in under three minutes.','The notification has been sworn in.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-16','one_human_notification_service','ONE HUMAN NOTIFICATION SERVICE','One person enters plans, remembers birthdays, catches conflicts, and then personally reminds the calendar’s other alleged user.','A shared calendar maintained by one person is a calendar-shaped assistant job. Update responsibility must follow the person making the plan or change.','The less active user adds their next three commitments and sets their own alerts. The maintainer stops issuing duplicate reminders unless requested. Agree that whoever creates or changes a plan updates it.','Push notifications will now push themselves.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-16','multiple_timelines_detected','MULTIPLE TIMELINES DETECTED','Plans exist across memory, texts, screenshots, and possibly a calendar last opened during onboarding.','The issue is not memory quality; it is lack of one trusted source. The Court orders migration before another double booking.','One partner creates the shared system and categories. The other imports upcoming commitments and confirms which alerts they will actually notice. Do a fifteen-minute calendar reset, then retire competing systems for shared plans.','Timeline merge completed with minor emotional downtime. ---','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-17','social_planning_duo','SOCIAL PLANNING DUO','Plans move from “we should” to an actual time because both people touch the process.','The Court finds shared social labor and unusually responsive group-chat behavior.','`[username A]` starts the next invite. `[username B]` closes the loop with time, place, or reservation. Plan one simple outing using only three messages each.','The poll may finally rest.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-17','organizer_plus_reliable_deputy','ORGANIZER PLUS RELIABLE DEPUTY','One person naturally conducts the group chat. The other does not lead but provides decisions, confirmations, and actual useful backup.','Different roles can be fair when the deputy is real, not ceremonial. Keep the organizer out of follow-up-message purgatory.','The organizer delegates one concrete step instead of doing it automatically. The deputy completes that step before being reminded. Split the next plan into invite, logistics, and confirmation.','Committee structure approved; meeting avoided.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-17','one_unpaid_event_coordinator','ONE UNPAID EVENT COORDINATOR','One person initiates, polls, reserves, confirms, and then receives “what time again?” from the person seated beside them.','Enjoying plans without sharing any planning is a convenience, not a personality type. The Court rotates ownership of the next outing.','The usual passenger plans the next social event end to end. The usual organizer supplies constraints once and resists taking the wheel back. Alternate full ownership for the next two plans.','“Keep me posted” has been denied as a complete contribution. ---','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-18','bins_under_control','BINS UNDER CONTROL','Trash exits on schedule, bags reappear, and the bins return from curbside travel.','The household sanitation system is functional. Maintain it with the humility appropriate to this achievement.','`[username A]` handles the next forgotten micro-step. `[username B]` checks supplies before the last bag becomes a crisis. Tie the task to one existing weekly habit.','The bins have rolled back into civilian life.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-18','one_sanitation_department','ONE SANITATION DEPARTMENT','One person has become calendar, collector, bag replacer, and curbside operations manager.','Taking out one full bag after being asked is not the same as owning trash day. Full-cycle responsibility transfers next week.','The new owner handles gathering through bin return. The usual owner does not issue reminders; the phone may accept that burden. Assign a permanent owner or visible weekly rotation.','Reminder services discontinued due to unpaid labor.','Warm, specific, lightly playful.'),
('LIFE-18','recurring_waste_management_thriller','RECURRING WASTE-MANAGEMENT THRILLER','Both people intend to handle it, each completes a different fragment, and the ending still features an approaching truck.','Good intentions require one named finish line. The Court separates indoor collection from outdoor timing and assigns both.','One partner owns all indoor bags and replacements. The other owns curb, pickup timing, and bin return. Set one shared alert with both roles written in the title.','Plot hole sealed with a fresh liner. --- # Conflict Court','Warm, specific, lightly playful.');
